      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update airflow to 3.3.1-2 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-71491 (GHSA-f2ff-p2ww-7p4p): before sqlparse 0.6.0, group_comments in sqlparse/engine/grouping.py rescanned comment-only statements repeatedly, so sqlparse.parse() or sqlparse.format(sql, strip_comments=True) on crafted input took quadratic CPU time. It is fixed in sqlparse 0.6.0 by commit ef2012a (https://github.com/andialbrecht/sqlparse/security/advisories/GHSA-f2ff-p2ww-7p4p, https://github.com/andialbrecht/sqlparse/commit/ef2012a5eeb491e604dea2b00d516904a3830c87). We listed every file of all 98 published airflow packages in the DHI Debian repository, 3.3.0-0 through the current 3.4.0-8, for amd64 and arm64 (no debug-symbol packages are published for this source), including the files inside the wheels they bundle, and read each library's version from its dist-info directory under /usr/lib/airflow/lib/python3.13/site-packages; both architectures agree for every build. Each build ships one copy of sqlparse, in site-packages: 0.5.5 in builds 3.3.0-0 to 3.3.1-1, 0.6.0 in 3.3.1-2 to 3.3.2-19, and 0.6.1 from 3.4.0-0 to the current 3.4.0-8, whose group_comments contains the early exit that commit adds. So builds before 3.3.1-2 are affected, and every build from 3.3.1-2 on carries the fix."
    },
